 Here's a JavaScript function that sorts a JSON object by its keys in alphabetical order, with ascending numerical values for keys that are numbers:

```javascript
function sortJsonObject(jsonObj) {
  // First, convert the JSON object to an array of key-value pairs using Object.entries()
  const entries = Object.entries(jsonObj);

  // Then, use Array.prototype.sort() to sort the entries based on the first element (key)
  entries.sort((a, b) => {
    if (typeof a[0] === 'string' && typeof b[0] === 'string') {
      return a[0].localeCompare(b[0]); // Compare strings alphabetically
    } else if (typeof a[0] === 'number' && typeof b[0] === 'number') {
      return a[0] - b[0]; // Compare numbers numerically
    } else {
      throw new Error('Invalid key type');
    }
  });

  // Finally, create a new JSON object from the sorted entries array
  return Object.fromEntries(entries);
}
```

