 To display a matrix as a bitmap with a zoom feature in Qt, you can follow these steps:

1. First, convert your matrix data into a QImage object. You can do this by creating a function that iterates through each element of the matrix and sets the corresponding pixel value in the QImage. Here's an example for a grayscale matrix:

```cpp
QImage matToImage(const int rows, const int cols, const float** data) {
    QImage image(cols, rows, QImage::Format_Graysc8);
    for (int i = 0; i < rows; ++i) {
        for (int j = 0; j < cols; ++j) {
            image.setPixelColor(j, i, QColor(qSqrt(data[i][j] * 255.0f));
        }
    }
    return image;
}
```

