<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Display Desktop Background</title>
    <style>
        #desktop-background {
            width: 100%;
            height: 100vh;
            background-size: cover;
            background-repeat: no-repeat;
            background-position: center;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <button onclick="getDesktopBackground()">Show Desktop Background</button>

    <div id="desktop-background"></div>

    <script>
        function getDesktopBackground() {
            if (document.body.style.backgroundImage) {
                document.getElementById("desktop-background").style.backgroundImage = document.body.style.backgroundImage;
            } else {
                const style = document.createElement('style');
                style.textContent = `
                    body {
                        background-image: ${window.getComputedStyle(document.body, null).backgroundImage};
                    }
                    #desktop-background {
                        display: block;
                    }
                `;
                document.head.appendChild(style);
                setTimeout(() => {
                    document.getElementById("desktop-background").style.backgroundImage = window.getComputedStyle(document.body, null).backgroundImage;
                    document.head.removeChild(style);
                }, 10);
            }
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This example creates a simple HTML page with a button that, when clicked, attempts to display the user's desktop background as the background image of the div element with the id "desktop-background". Keep in mind that this solution might not be perfect due to browser compatibility issues

