if randomise is false, then the index of the item in the array should be item.position-1
whereas if randomize is true, the item can be placed anywhere in the resultant array

response:
 To create a new array based on the given conditions, you can follow these steps:

1. Create an empty result array with enough capacity to hold all elements from the input array.
2. Iterate through each element in the input array.
3. If `randomize` is `false`, add the element at the index `item.position - 1` in the result array.
4. If `randomize` is `true`, find an available index in the result array and add the element there.

Here's a code example in JavaScript:

```javascript
function createNewArray(input) {
  const result = new Array(Math.max(...input.map((i) => i.position)));
  let currentIndex = 0;

  for (const item of input) {
    if (!item.randomize) {
      result[item.position - 1] = item.name;
    } else {
      while (result[currentIndex]) {
        currentIndex++;
      }
      result[currentIndex] = item.name;
    }
  }

  return result;
}
```

